  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1216 AM EST Thu Nov 19 2026\n\nUpper ridging aloft along with broad surface high pressure over the \nregion will keep above normal temperatures and dry conditions in \nplace through much of the weekend. The next chance of rain looks to \nbe a weak front moving into the forecast area from the west Sunday \nnight into Monday. Deterministic guidance shows only a modest \nincrease in PWATs just ahead of the front due to a loose connection \nto moisture from the far western Gulf. Combine the weak moisture \nreturn with waning upper support as it approaches, and I wouldn't \nexpect much out of it with respect to rain amounts or coverage to be \nhonest. \n\nOtherwise, the main concern for the coming days will be continued \nlow afternoon RH values. Once again NBM is entirely too high with \ndewpoints tomorrow and likely Friday afternoon as well. Blended in a \nhealthy dose of CONSShort and HRRR to arrive at afternoon RH below \n30 percent across much of the area today, with similar values Friday \nas well although slightly higher. The lowest RH values will be in \nthe north both days. On the positive side, winds will be light.\n\nDrier and slightly cooler air will move in behind the front Monday \nand Tuesday, with temperatures back down closer to seasonal normals. \nModels are in very poor agreement by the end of the period, but the \nensemble approach yields a chance of rain moving back into our area \nby Wednesday.",
